    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s highest efficiency score at 73.17. While he faces Painter, the combination of a favorable park factor and a top-of-the-order assignment makes him our primary anchor. Similarly, **Geraldo Perdomo** (72.66) and **Taylor Ward** (71.46) are must-starts. **Geraldo Perdomo** benefits significantly from a soft matchup against Quintana, where his ability to capitalize on the lefty-lefty dynamic\u2014coupled with our aggressive pursuit of the scarce SB category\u2014elevates his value. **Taylor Ward** remains in an elite tier today thanks to an impressive BvP history against Valdez and favorable park dimensions that bolster his home run upside. **Daulton Varsho** (69.53) also finds himself in a prime spot; despite the presence of a strong catcher behind the plate, his platoon advantage against Keller makes him one of our most efficient producers.\n\nThe decision to keep **Jonathan Aranda** (45.21) on the bench was the most difficult call of the morning. While he maintains a strong xwOBA, the negative impact of facing Weathers, combined with detrimental wind conditions, pushed his efficiency score well below our other infield options. We are also monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" statuses closely, specifically for **Luis Arraez** and **Matt Chapman**. Both are currently projected at 60.28 and 59.64 respectively, largely buoyed by a favorable wind forecast and the weak 4.95 xERA of Schultz; however, should these players shift lower in their respective lineups, those efficiency scores will require re-evaluation. \n\nWhile we are optimized for maximum output, we must remain wary of the risks associated with the lower end of our card. **Lawrence Butler** carries a score of 54.09, which is heavily reliant on his platoon advantage against King; should he be tucked into the nine-hole as anticipated, the resulting lack of RBI opportunities creates a lower floor that we will be monitoring closely throughout the evening. We are also keeping a close eye on **Jeremiah Jackson** (50.20). While his raw score is marginal, his 100% SB potential against the slow delivery of Valdez makes him a tactical play despite his lower lineup placement. Finally, we continue to hold **Cal Raleigh** on the IL, as he remains unavailable for selection.",
